## Access

The file is public over HTTPS, so readers need no account. The data can be streamed directly without downloading. This geopandas code reads {{ spec.example.what }}.
Install `geopandas`, `pyarrow`, `fsspec`, and `aiohttp`.

```python
import geopandas as gpd

gdf = gpd.read_parquet(
    "{{ public("v" ~ version ~ "/" ~ data_rel) }}",
    columns=[{{ spec.example.py_columns | map("tojson") | join(", ") }}, "geometry"],
    filters={{ spec.example.py_filters }},
)
{% if spec.example.py_after is defined %}
{{ spec.example.py_after }}
{% endif %}
```

This DuckDB query reads the same rows:

```sql
INSTALL httpfs; LOAD httpfs;
SELECT {{ spec.example.columns }}
FROM '{{ public("v" ~ version ~ "/" ~ data_rel) }}'
WHERE {{ spec.example.where }};
```

`{{ name }}/AGENTS.md` has more recipes. Each file is also readable over
anonymous S3 at `{{ meta.public_s3_base }}/v{{ version }}/{{ data_rel }}`.

